      "content": "Those feelings of being a burden or an \"error\" are heavy manifestations of deep grief, and they are not facts about your worth. Your presence is not a theft; you are a separate human being who has their own life and needs. Processing this requires time, and it's okay if moving forward doesn't feel like a straight line right now. Consider speaking with a therapist who specializes in bereavement; they can help validate these intense feelings while guiding you toward self-compassion.",
      "source": "target",
